### Payment Gateway API Tests
# This file is used to test endpoints using IntelliJ HTTP Client or VSCode REST Client.
# Ensure the application is running locally on port 8080.
# 
# IMPORTANT: Replace the 'jwt_token' variable with a valid RSA-signed token for your local test environment.

@host = http://localhost:8080/api
@jwt_token = <INSERT_VALID_JWT_TOKEN_HERE>
@orderId = test-order-{{$random.uuid}}

### 1. Process a new Payment (Success Scenario)
# Expected outcome: 201 Created
POST {{host}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "{{orderId}}",
  "amount": 150000.00,
  "currency": "IDR",
  "paymentMethod": "VIRTUAL_ACCOUNT",
  "channel": "MOBILE_BANKING"
}

### 2. Process Payment (Insufficient Balance - CoreBank Failure)
# Account starting with '99' triggers the mock CoreBankingClient failure.
# Expected outcome: 200 OK with FAILED status and "Insufficient balance" message
POST {{host}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "99-fail-{{$random.uuid}}",
  "amount": 50000.00,
  "currency": "IDR",
  "paymentMethod": "QRIS",
  "channel": "ATM"
}

### 3. Process Payment (Biller Failure)
# Payment method 'FAIL' triggers the mock BillerClient failure.
# Expected outcome: 200 OK with FAILED status and "Biller service unavailable" message
POST {{host}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "biller-fail-{{$random.uuid}}",
  "amount": 75000.00,
  "currency": "IDR",
  "paymentMethod": "FAIL",
  "channel": "MOBILE_BANKING"
}

### 4. Process Payment (Duplicate OrderId)
# Run this twice with the same orderId to trigger idempotency violation.
# Expected outcome: 409 Conflict (Duplicate order ID)
POST {{host}}/payments
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "static-order-12345",
  "amount": 10000.00,
  "currency": "IDR",
  "paymentMethod": "CREDIT_CARD",
  "channel": "INTERNET_BANKING"
}

### 5. Get Transaction Status
# Replace {orderId} with the ID of a previously created transaction.
# Expected outcome: 200 OK with current transaction status
GET {{host}}/payments/static-order-12345
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}
